# Shared Material

This directory holds relatively stable material reused by multiple tasks. Anything that only serves one work episode belongs in `.project/`; see the root `TODO.md` for the task index.

## Numbering Convention

- The two-digit prefix only controls ordering, not importance; categories start at `01`, and `00` may be reserved for overview, glossary, or project-background material
- `01-environments/` is the fixed slot for per-environment access details; the "Environment Index" in `CLAUDE.md` points here
- Append new categories at the end of the numbering; never renumber and never reuse a removed number
- Organize inside a category by sub-topic or filename — **do not use `YYYYMMDD-` date directories**
- When several versions of a document exist, keep only the latest and record the version in the filename or the body

## Index

| No. | Category directory | Contents |
|-----|--------------------|----------|
| 00 | `00-overview/` (optional) | Project background, glossary, overall architecture |
| 01 | `01-environments/` (fixed) | Environment and access details: `test.md` / `uat.md` / `prd.md`; only for environments that exist |
| 02 | `02-{{CATEGORY}}/` | {{SHARED_MATERIAL_IN_THIS_CATEGORY}} |
| 03 | `03-{{CATEGORY}}/` | {{SHARED_MATERIAL_IN_THIS_CATEGORY}} |

## Maintenance

- Update the table above and the "Environment Index" in `CLAUDE.md` whenever you add, move, or split a category
- Keep each shared document and its attachments in exactly one place; `.project/` topic directories link to them with relative paths instead of copying
- Shared is not the same as publishable; check scope and sensitive content before sending anything outside the team
